{
  "week": 1,
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "w1-l1",
      "week": 1,
      "order": 1,
      "title": "Seven sounds, one shape",
      "goal": "Meet the ለ family one vowel at a time, then see the same marks on መ.",
      "newFamilies": [
        "ለ",
        "መ"
      ],
      "estimatedMinutes": 12,
      "cultureNote": "Ethiopian children learn the fidel by chanting each family across its seven orders: ሀ ሁ ሂ ሃ ሄ ህ ሆ. The app's 'chant' button does the same.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "type": "intro",
          "text": "Amharic letters come in families: one shape, changed a little for each vowel. Today you'll meet one family, step by step — just listening and looking. No writing yet."
        },
        {
          "type": "hear",
          "items": [
            "ለ"
          ],
          "text": "This is ለ — \"le\". It's the base shape of the l family."
        },
        {
          "type": "hear",
          "items": [
            "ለ",
            "ሉ",
            "ሊ",
            "ላ"
          ],
          "text": "Add a small mark and the vowel changes. Here are the first four: le, lu, li, la."
        },
        {
          "type": "see",
          "family": "ለ",
          "orders": [
            1,
            2,
            3,
            4
          ],
          "title": "Four forms",
          "text": "ሉ has a little foot for u. ሊ has a leg for i. ላ lowers its leg for a. The gold shows each mark."
        },
        {
          "type": "exercise",
          "kind": "soundMatch",
          "prompt": "ሉ",
          "options": [
            "ለ",
            "ሉ",
            "ሊ",
            "ላ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "soundKey",
          "title": "Three more sounds",
          "text": "Two of them are written with letters you may not know: ē and ə. Tap each one to hear it.",
          "items": [
            {
              "char": "ሌ",
              "hint": "ē — like the “ay” in “say”"
            },
            {
              "char": "ል",
              "hint": "ə — a very short vowel, sometimes not said at all"
            },
            {
              "char": "ሎ",
              "hint": "o — like the “o” in “go”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "see",
          "family": "ለ",
          "orders": [
            5,
            6,
            7
          ],
          "title": "Three more forms",
          "text": "ሌ has a ring for ē. ል bends its stem for ə. ሎ has a loop for o."
        },
        {
          "type": "exercise",
          "kind": "soundMatch",
          "prompt": "ሎ",
          "options": [
            "ሌ",
            "ል",
            "ሎ",
            "ሊ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "see",
          "family": "ለ",
          "title": "The whole family",
          "text": "Seven forms, one shape. Tap any of them to hear it again."
        },
        {
          "type": "chant",
          "family": "ለ"
        },
        {
          "type": "rule",
          "title": "Same marks, new letter",
          "text": "Here's a second family, መ — \"me\". You've never seen it, but you already know its marks."
        },
        {
          "type": "see",
          "family": "መ",
          "title": "The መ family",
          "text": "Look for the same foot, leg, ring and loop you just learned."
        },
        {
          "type": "exercise",
          "kind": "gridFill",
          "family": "መ",
          "hide": [
            2,
            4
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "exercise",
          "kind": "soundMatch",
          "prompt": "ሚ",
          "options": [
            "ሚ",
            "ሊ",
            "ማ",
            "ሙ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "wrapUp",
          "text": "You can already read 14 characters. Next time: writing and saying them, plus አ and ሰ — and your first words."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "w1-l2",
      "week": 1,
      "order": 2,
      "title": "Hello, name, mother",
      "goal": "Write and say your first letters, then add አ and ሰ and read real words.",
      "newFamilies": [
        "አ",
        "ሰ"
      ],
      "estimatedMinutes": 20,
      "cultureNote": "ሰላም (selam) means peace. It is the everyday greeting — and many Ethiopian girls are named Selam.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "type": "review"
        },
        {
          "type": "intro",
          "text": "Today you'll write and say the letters you met last time, then add two families — አ and ሰ — and read your first real words."
        },
        {
          "type": "trace",
          "chars": [
            "ለ",
            "ላ",
            "ሎ",
            "መ",
            "ማ",
            "ም"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "say",
          "items": [
            "ለ",
            "ሉ",
            "ሊ",
            "ላ",
            "ሌ",
            "ል",
            "ሎ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "hear",
          "items": [
            "አ",
            "ኡ",
            "ኢ",
            "ኣ",
            "ኤ",
            "እ",
            "ኦ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "see",
          "family": "አ",
          "title": "A letter for vowels",
          "text": "አ is different: it has no consonant of its own, so each form is just a vowel — a, u, i, a, ē, ə, o. The first and fourth forms both sound like “a”."
        },
        {
          "type": "hear",
          "items": [
            "ሰ",
            "ሱ",
            "ሲ",
            "ሳ",
            "ሴ",
            "ስ",
            "ሶ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "see",
          "family": "ሰ"
        },
        {
          "type": "rule",
          "title": "The 6th order does double duty",
          "text": "ስ and ም can be 'sə'/'mə' or just 's'/'m' with no vowel. So ስም is 'səm' (name), not 'sə-mə'."
        },
        {
          "type": "trace",
          "chars": [
            "ሰ",
            "ሳ",
            "ስ",
            "አ",
            "እ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "words",
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "selam",
              "amharic": "ሰላም",
              "roman": "selam",
              "english": "hello / peace",
              "picture": "🕊️",
              "audio": "/audio/words/selam.mp3",
              "reviewed": false
            },
            {
              "id": "səm",
              "amharic": "ስም",
              "roman": "səm",
              "english": "name",
              "picture": "🏷️",
              "audio": "/audio/words/səm.mp3",
              "reviewed": false
            },
            {
              "id": "əmama",
              "amharic": "እማማ",
              "roman": "əmama",
              "english": "mom",
              "picture": "👩",
              "audio": "/audio/words/əmama.mp3",
              "reviewed": false
            },
            {
              "id": "semma",
              "amharic": "ሰማ",
              "roman": "semma",
              "english": "he heard",
              "picture": "👂",
              "audio": "/audio/words/semma.mp3",
              "reviewed": false,
              "note": "Doubling! The m is held longer — listen closely. Writing doesn't show it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "exercise",
          "kind": "buildWord",
          "target": "ሰላም",
          "tiles": [
            "ላ",
            "ም",
            "ሰ",
            "ሊ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "exercise",
          "kind": "minimalPair",
          "note": "Hear the held m",
          "a": {
            "id": "semma",
            "amharic": "ሰማ",
            "roman": "semma",
            "english": "he heard",
            "picture": "👂",
            "audio": "/audio/words/semma.mp3",
            "reviewed": false
          },
          "b": {
            "id": "sema",
            "amharic": "ሰማ",
            "roman": "sema",
            "english": "(no doubling)",
            "picture": "🔈",
            "audio": "/audio/words/sema.mp3",
            "reviewed": false,
            "note": "Contrast audio only — record a short m."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "exercise",
          "kind": "dictation",
          "target": "ስም"
        },
        {
          "type": "say",
          "items": [
            "ሰላም",
            "እማማ",
            "ስም"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "wrapUp",
          "text": "Four families, four real words. Tomorrow: በ, and you'll read a mini story."
        }
      ]
    },
